    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1063">

                <pb facs="0797" n="721" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg721"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.63/168</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Special Representative
                        Rodgers </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-20T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 20, 1916, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>86. Silliman reports Governor Zacatecas decreed all mine owners must begin
                    working within 30 days; otherwise laborers permitted work mines their own
                    account.</p>
                <p>Take up with appropriate authorities behalf American mine owners, pointing out
                    impossibility their working mines under present disturbed conditions and absence
                    transportation facilities. Endeavor obtain withdrawal decree.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
